{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[B]I wish I'd [B]never come back [B]home[B]
[B]It don't feel [B]right since I've been [F#]grown[C#][F#]
[B]I can't find [B7]any of my [E]old friends hanging [E7]around
Won't [B]nothing bring you [F#]down like your [B]hometown[B]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I spent some time in New Orleans
I had to live on rice and beans
I hitched through Texas when the sun was beating down
Won't nothing bring you down like your hometown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]Home is where the [E]heart is
Ain't that [B]what they always [B]say?
[C#/E#]My heart lies in [C#/E#]broken pieces
[F#]Scattered [C#]along the [F#7]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
So don't think about me when I'm gone
I don't mind traveling alone
You are the sweetest little thing that I ever found
Won't nothing bring you down like your hometown
{end_of_verse}

